First Author: Tran-Dinh
Title: Early identification of high-risk individuals for mortality after lung transplantation: A retrospective cohort study with topological feature engineering
Source number: 71

Very short summary: This retrospective single-center study included 252 consecutive adult lung transplant recipients treated in Paris, France, between 2015 and 2020. A multilayer perceptron integrating clinical variables with 27 persistent-homology-derived topological features was evaluated using nested stratified cross-validation; the full model achieved an AUC of 0.87 (95% CI 0.81–0.93), with detailed performance tables reporting 90% accuracy, 84% sensitivity, and 90% specificity for 1-year mortality prediction.

