	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The primary classifier was a regularized MLP using 49 clinical variables and 27 topological features generated from persistent-homology representations. It was compared with the Lung Transplant Risk Index, Charlson Comorbidity Index, FEV1, clinical-only MLP, random forest, gradient boosting, logistic regression, and other classifiers. Validation used nested stratified cross-validation with five outer folds for performance estimation and three inner folds for hyperparameter tuning. Recursive feature elimination with cross-validation was performed within each training fold, retaining a mean of 34 ± 6 features. SHAP, partial-dependence plots, effect sizes, and an interpretable risk score were used for explanation.

